  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/model_routing.py, `_run_delegated_codex`: `except BaseException: closed = close_attempt(...); _write_route(...); raise`. `close_attempt` computes `task_content_post` via `_task_content_state`, which raises `RoutingError` when the snapshot or identity cannot be established. The same call also precedes `_write_route` on the success path. Capturing the post-state defensively, or writing a closed attempt without it, would keep the original error visible and the delegation state consistent.",
      "id": "codex-close-attempt-masks-failure",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "In `_run_delegated_codex`, the failure handler calls `close_attempt(...)`, which calls `_task_content_state(...)`. That call can raise `RoutingError`. If it does, the original launch error is lost and the route is not rewritten, so the Codex delegation stays `open`."
    }
  ],
